own rv" href="/rhode-island-communities/woonsocket/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/woonsocket-mill.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/woonsocket-mill-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/woonsocket-mill.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 280px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span><b>Woonsocket</b><small>Providence County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/rhode-island-communities/newport/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/newport-harbor.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/newport-harbor-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/newport-harbor.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 280px" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span><b>Newport</b><small>Newport County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/rhode-island-communities/westerly/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/westerly-beach.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/westerly-beach-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/westerly-beach.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 280px" width="1200" height="797" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span><b>Westerly</b><small>Washington County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/rhode-island-communities/narragansett/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/point-judith-light.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/point-judith-light-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/point-judith-light.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 280px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span><b>Narragansett</b><small>Washington County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/rhode-island-communities/bristol/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/bristol-harbor.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/bristol-harbor-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/bristol-harbor.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 280px" width="960" height="638" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span><b>Bristol</b><small>Bristol County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/rhode-island-communities/north-kingstown/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/wickford-village.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/wickford-village-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/wickford-village.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 280px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span><b>North Kingstown</b><small>Washington County</small></span></a><a class="town rv" href="/rhode-island-communities/coventry/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/ri-farm-field.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/ri-farm-field-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/ri-farm-field.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 280px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span><b>Coventry</b><small>Kent County</small></span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="sec stone"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head rv"><div><p class="tag dark">Regions</p><h2>How claims differ across Rhode Island</h2></div><p>The same policy language plays out very differently on a barrier beach, in a mill city and in the northwest hills.</p></div><div class="pgrid"><div class="pcard static rv"><span class="pcard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/providence-college-hill.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/providence-college-hill-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/providence-college-hill.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="pcard-k">Providence · Pawtucket · Woonsocket</span></span><span class="pcard-b"><h2>Providence &amp; Blackstone Valley</h2><p>The state’s densest housing: three-deckers, Victorian homes and converted mills. Winter water losses and fires that spread between buildings are common, and older materials push repair costs up.</p><p class="small">Providence, Pawtucket, Central Falls, Woonsocket, Cumberland, Lincoln, North Providence</p></span></div><div class="pcard static rv"><span class="pcard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/warwick-shore.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/warwick-shore-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/warwick-shore.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="pcard-k">Warwick · Cranston · Coventry</span></span><span class="pcard-b"><h2>Kent County &amp; West Bay</h2><p>Postwar neighborhoods, bay shoreline and the Pawtuxet River. The March 2010 floods still shape how owners here think about water, and wooded streets mean trees on houses after big storms.</p><p class="small">Warwick, Cranston, West Warwick, Coventry, East Greenwich, West Greenwich</p></span></div><div class="pcard static rv"><span class="pcard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/bristol-harbor.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/bristol-harbor-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/bristol-harbor.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="960" height="638" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="pcard-k">East Providence · Barrington · Bristol</span></span><span class="pcard-b"><h2>East Bay</h2><p>Low-lying peninsulas and long bay frontage. Hurricanes in 1938 and 1954 flooded these towns, and historic downtowns in Bristol and Warren add material-matching questions.</p><p class="small">East Providence, Barrington, Warren, Bristol</p></span></div><div class="pcard static rv"><span class="pcard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/newport-harbor.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/newport-harbor-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/newport-harbor.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="pcard-k">Newport · Middletown · Portsmouth</span></span><span class="pcard-b"><h2>Newport County</h2><p>Aquidneck Island and the eastern shore face the Atlantic. Colonial and Gilded Age buildings, estate homes and shoreline exposure make claims here detailed and expensive.</p><p class="small">Newport, Middletown, Portsmouth, Jamestown, Tiverton, Little Compton</p></span></div><div class="pcard static rv"><span class="pcard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/westerly-beach.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/westerly-beach-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/westerly-beach.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1200" height="797" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="pcard-k">Westerly · Narragansett · North Kingstown</span></span><span class="pcard-b"><h2>South County &amp; Block Island</h2><p>Barrier beaches, salt ponds and summer communities. The 1938 hurricane, Sandy in 2012 and Henri in 2021 all struck this coast. Hurricane deductibles and wind-versus-flood questions come up on almost every claim.</p><p class="small">Westerly, Charlestown, South Kingstown, Narragansett, North Kingstown, New Shoreham (Block Island)</p></span></div><div class="pcard static rv"><span class="pcard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/snow-roof.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/snow-roof-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/snow-roof.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="960" height="640" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="pcard-k">Glocester · Scituate · Burrillville</span></span><span class="pcard-b"><h2>Northwest Hills</h2><p>Higher ground, deep woods and the Scituate Reservoir. More snow than the coast, long outages after storms, and rural properties with barns, wells and long driveways.</p><p class="small">Burrillville, Glocester, Foster, Scituate, Smithfield, North Smithfield</p></span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="strip"><div class="wrap strip-in rv"><div><h2>Don’t see your town?</h2><p>We work in all 39 cities and towns. Call and tell us where the property is.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn ink" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn ink-line" href="/request-a-claim-review/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
